{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548794-fractured-tzimisce-based-on-revenants","id":1548794,"title":"Fractured Tzimisce based on Revenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-26T11:25:07-08:00","id":1548794,"title":"Fractured Tzimisce based on Revenants","content":"So this is an alternative version of the Tzimisce that I think might be interesting and I wanted some input.<br /> <br /> Imagine if at some point in the past, maybe the Anarch Revolts which shook up all the Clans, the Tzimisce Clan fractured into factions based on the Revenant families. Maybe the chaos and deaths caused the revolts lead to a collapse of the Clan and only those families and their members who had been embraced had the stability to survive.<br /> <br /> Then the various Revenant Bloodlines joined different Sects, some in the Camarilla, some in the Sabbat, and some independent.<br /> <br /> How do y\u2019all think that this scenario would play out? Which Bloodlines would be in which Sects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T02:30:31-08:00","id":1548811,"title":"","content":"Cool idea!<br /> <br /> The only thing I can say right now is that with the exception of the Grimaldi I don't think that any family would join the Camarilla. They are to divorced from humanity and to much of a risk for the Masquerade to be accepted, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Thus you would probably find most in the Sabbat with a few independent ones. The whole &quot;Road of Humanity is the only game in town!&quot; thing with the Camarilla would probably work as badly with a fractured Tzimisce as with the vanilla Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> And that's without taking into account the enemity with the Tremere and Ventrue, the actions during the Anarch Revolt and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T12:11:51-08:00","id":1548821,"title":"","content":"Agree that this is an interesting idea, for sure. I also think that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> is correct about the Grimaldi joining the Camarilla while most of the other Families would still end up in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I think that the Obertus are the most likely to end up as Independent. While their research often ignores ethical boundaries, they aren't as barbaric as the Bratovitches or as depraved as the Zantosas. I could see them mostly just wanting to be left alone, hiring out their scholarly talents when it suits them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T11:52:19-08:00","id":1548849,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Szantovich family could have fit into the Camarilla. But then perhaps they wouldn't have much a niche there if the Camarilla Tzimisce were more mortal-passing. They might be treated as more of a liability in the Camarilla, but that could be said about any revenant family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T19:26:15-08:00","id":1548860,"title":"","content":"Alright, here is one possible option. I\u2019m going to put a few families into each faction.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bratovitch</b><br /> The Bratovitch are serves the Sabbat in the wild areas outside of civilization. They make up the majority of nomadic Tzimisce. Their extremely violent and bestowal nature makes them ill suited for city life or intrigues.<br /> <br /> <b>Grimaldi</b><br /> Ironically, the most human and \u201cwell adjusted\u201d family serves the Sabbat. They are masters of business and dealing with mortal institutions. A skill which makes them extremely valuable to the Sabbat who often eschew temporal power and connections.<br /> <br /> <b>Krevcheski</b><br /> The Krevcheski are the modern Sabbat Tzimisce as we most often imagine them. Twisted and sadistic, they delight in torture and experimentation, they seek to transcend their vampiric forms and often change their shapes in inhuman ways. They have a scientific outlook and like technology as well as biological experimentation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Camarilla</b><br /> <br /> <b>Zantosa</b><br /> There debauched nobles delight in hedonism and perversity, but their are also highly skilled in the social arena and value their noble lineage and connections. In the Camarilla they keep their darker practices a secret while using their aristocratic connections and charisma to influence mortal society.<br /> <br /> <b>Vlaszy</b><br /> The Vlaszy were the devoted servants of the Tzimisce elders in time past. They hold absolute adherence to honor in highest regard. They were nearly destroyed by the Anarchs but managed to survive and protect their elder masters. Within the Camarilla, they are staunch conservatives who side with elder rule and adherence to the traditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Danislav</b>\u200b<br /> This family are known for their connection to wild places, they are lords of the land that command both mortal and animal servants. Their wild domains often isolate them from Camarilla city politics but their adherence to tradition and loyalty to their elders lead them to ally with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Independent </b><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Obertus</b>\u200b<br /> The Obertus family had little use for the politics of the Camarilla or Sabbat. They preferred to study arcane secrets and experiment with the undead state. They largely keep to themselves, but will deal with other Clans from time to often, often buying or selling forbidden knowledge.<br /> <br /> <b>Khazi</b>\u200b<br /> This bizarre family of albinos has no place in the Sabbat or Camarilla. They still serve their Methuselah founder with religious devotion in secret sanctuaries hidden away from kindred and kine alike. \u200bThey are willing to ally with other Clans or bloodlines if they believe it serves their purposes. They Sabbat despise them for their devotion to an elder while the Camarilla is wary because of their strange appearance and behavior.<br /> <br /> <b>Basarab</b>\u200b<br /> The infamous family which produced Dracula. These Tzimisce bowed to no Sect and still commands their ancient homes in the Carpathians. They are known for their skill in dark magic and utter ruthlessness. \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}